<font size="+1"><b>Survey: Execs rethinking IT budgets</b></a></font><br>

Growing numbers of <b>Fortune 1000 CIOs</b> are re-evaluating their IT budgets and spending plans for coming months, according to a recent survey. Morgan Stanley finds that CIOs' top priorities include security software, application integration and Windows 2000/XP upgrades for the desktop. <b>Integration challenges</b> were slowing the rate of application adoption for 38 percent of those surveyed.

